Copyright © 2026 Gautech. All rights reserved.

mandarinmaxxing is free, and it stays free. You're welcome to study with it, read
how it's made, and help make it better.

This license is here for one reason: to protect what this project and its community
build. It keeps the maps and the lesson texts from being copied into other products,
or fed to an AI to mass-produce imitations.

WHAT THIS COVERS

The lesson maps, the skill's instructions and texts, and the code in this repository.
Material that comes from others keeps its own terms: the HSK word lists and the Hanzi
font, listed under "Credits" in the README.

YOU CAN

- Install the skill and study with it, for as long as you like.
- Change your own copy to suit the way you study.
- Read everything, and share the link to the project.
- Borrow the method. Grouping words by situation, teaching chunks, bringing old
  words back: ideas aren't covered by this license. Build your own from scratch.

YOU CAN'T, WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION

- Republish or redistribute this material, in whole or in part, changed or not.
- Use it to make or improve another skill, course, app, dataset or product, free or
  paid. That includes giving it to an AI system to produce one.
- Sell it.

FREE, AND IT STAYS FREE

The skill in this repository is free, and stays free. Whatever Gautech builds later,
this skill will not be put behind a price.

IF YOU CONTRIBUTE

Thank you. When you send a fix, a map or a text, you remain its author, and you give
Gautech a permanent, worldwide, royalty-free license to use, change, publish and
sublicense it as part of the project and of anything built from it. You confirm it
is yours to give. Everyone who contributes is credited in CONTRIBUTORS.md.

NO WARRANTY

This material is provided as is, with no warranty of any kind.

